    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is headlined by **Corbin Carroll**, who commands an elite score of 87.14 against the vulnerable Randy V\u00e1squez. With an expected ERA of 4.92, V\u00e1squez provides the perfect environment for **Corbin Carroll** to utilize his elite sprint speed to chase stolen bases, which remain our primary scarcity target. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.13) project as top-tier starts today. **Mickey Moniak** specifically benefits from a massive 14% boost due to favorable park factors and a strong platoon alignment against Freddy Peralta, while **Tyler Soderstrom** sits in a high-leverage #3 hole against a middling arm in Brady Singer, offering significant upside for both power and run production.\n\nOn the periphery of the lineup, **Josh Naylor** (59.34) and **Austin Riley** (58.16) hover in the marginal-to-strong territory. **Austin Riley** receives a subtle bump from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery (88% SB efficiency), which provides a unique edge despite his lower spot in the order. The most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana** (37.71), who fell just shy of our 40.0 floor due to a disadvantageous lefty-lefty platoon matchup against Sean Manaea. While **Travis Bazzana** remains a high-upside prospect, the current projections suggest his efficiency is better preserved on the pine today. \n\nWe are monitoring one significant hurdle: **Seiya Suzuki** is drawing a tough assignment against the formidable Tarik Skubal (2.67 xERA). While **Seiya Suzuki** is currently cleared to start based on his baseline, his score of 50.49 reflects the significant risk posed by Skubal\u2019s elite strikeout ability. We are keeping a close watch on weather reports for any late-breaking developments, but for now, the optimizer favors the aggressive deployment of **Corbin Carroll**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Tyler Soderstrom** to push our counting categories forward.",
